IMPORT prelude

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2014 (NSW) -- the claims and costs provisions a client meets, from the
-- seat of the client: the person bringing or answering a claim (usually the injured person claiming personal injury
-- damages) and paying, or being paid, legal costs.
--
-- SEAT: the client. Every exported question is one the client would ask: "Does the maximum costs limit apply to my
-- claim?", "What is the most my lawyers can charge?", "Can I be made to pay the other side more?", "Can my lawyers act
-- on a claim with no reasonable prospects?", "Can I apply for costs assessment, and by when must I seek a review?",
-- "Can I claim against the Fidelity Fund?". Law practices, courts, costs assessors, the Manager, Costs Assessment and
-- the Law Society Council get no seat: what they must or may do is encoded as what it means for the client.
--
-- Provisions: s 4 (the Uniform Law applies as NSW law, so its own terms are asked as facts); s 59(2) (fixed costs);
-- Sch 1 (maximum costs in personal injury damages matters, cll 1-8, via s 61); Sch 2 (costs where no reasonable
-- prospects of success, cll 1-6, via s 62); Part 7 (costs assessment: ss 63, 66, 68(3), 70(4)-(5), 74(1), 81, 83, 86,
-- 89, 90); Part 9 Div 2 (claims about defaults, ss 122, 124). Out (see NOTES.md): Part 1 machinery, Part 2 Div 2,
-- Parts 3-5, Part 8, Part 9 Div 1, Parts 10-13, Schedules 3-10.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a flat "does not apply",
-- "cannot", "must not ... unless", a condition introduced by "if", a period the text fixes), or NOTHING where the Act
-- does not answer on the facts given; each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Judgments the Act leaves to a
-- court, a costs assessor or the Manager, Costs Assessment are asked as inputs, never decided here.
--
-- Figures: the Act's own ($100,000, $10,000, 20%, $7,500, 15%, $25,000, $100,000, 30 days). The local regulations may
-- replace the Schedule 1 figures (cll 2(2), 3(5)); they are not deposited, so the Act's figures are used.
--
-- Dates use only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL), not the daydate library.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2014`

§§ `The nouns`

-- Sch 1 cl 1(1) "plaintiff means a person who makes or is entitled to make a claim for personal injury damages";
-- "defendant means a person against whom a claim for personal injury damages is or may be made".
DECLARE `My side of the claim` IS ONE OF
    `the plaintiff`
    `the defendant`

-- Sch 1 cl 1(2): the claims whose costs the Schedule does not apply to. The Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 is not
-- named (finding 1, fork F2).
DECLARE `Kind of personal injury claim` IS ONE OF
    `a claim under the Motor Accidents Act 1988 or the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999`
    `a claim for work injury damages`
    `a dust diseases claim of the kind in section 11 of the Dust Diseases Tribunal Act 1989`
    `a claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017`
    `another claim for personal injury damages`

-- The answer to "what are the maximum costs?" (Sch 1 cll 2, 3, 7).
DECLARE `Maximum costs answer` IS ONE OF
    `the maximum costs are` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `Schedule 1 fixes no maximum for this claim`
    `the Act does not settle it`

-- Sch 2 cl 4(4) "court documentation".
DECLARE `Kind of court document` IS ONE OF
    `an originating process, defence or further pleading`
    `an amended originating process, defence or further pleading`
    `a document amending an originating process, defence or further pleading`
    `another document of a kind the local regulations prescribe`
    `any other document`

-- The answer to "can the court make my law practice repay the costs I was ordered to pay?" (Sch 2 cll 5, 6).
DECLARE `Repayment order answer` IS ONE OF
    `the court may order my law practice to repay those costs`
    `the court cannot make that order on these facts`
    `it is too late to apply for that order`
    `Schedule 2 does not reach my claim`

-- Who a person is in relation to ordered costs (s 74(1)).
DECLARE `My position on the ordered costs` IS ONE OF
    `I have paid or am liable to pay them`
    `I have received or am entitled to receive them`
    `neither`

-- The answer to "is my application for review in time?" (s 83).
DECLARE `Review application answer` IS ONE OF
    `my application for review is in time`
    `the time for applying for review has passed`
    `the certificate has not been forwarded yet, so the 30 days have not begun`

-- The answer to "can I appeal the review panel's decision?" (s 89(1)).
DECLARE `Appeal answer` IS ONE OF
    `I can appeal without leave`
    `I can appeal only with the court's leave`
    `section 89 gives me no appeal`

DECLARE `Appeal court` IS ONE OF
    `the District Court`
    `the Supreme Court`

-- The parties and act of the one regulative rule (s 83(1)).
DECLARE `Costs party` IS ONE OF `the party to the costs assessment`
DECLARE `Costs act` IS ONE OF `apply for a review of the determination`

§§ `Arithmetic and dates`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b
    THEN a
    ELSE b

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS n)

§§ `s 59 -- fixed costs`

-- s 59(2) "A law practice is not entitled to be paid or recover for a legal service an amount that exceeds the fair and
-- reasonable cost fixed for the service by the regulations under this section." A flat negative: over the fixed cost,
-- JUST TRUE (it is barred); at or under it, s 59(2) does not bar the charge (JUST FALSE), though the Uniform Law's own
-- fair-and-reasonable test still applies. With no fixed cost, s 59(2) says nothing (NOTHING). The local regulations
-- under s 59(1) are not deposited: whether they fix a cost, and its amount, are inputs. Sch 1 cl 2(7): the Schedule 1
-- maximum applies despite a fixed cost for personal injury damages.
@export Does a fixed cost set by the regulations stop my law practice from charging me this amount for a legal service (s 59(2))?
GIVEN `the regulations fix a cost for this legal service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the NSW local regulations under s 59 fix a fair and reasonable cost for the legal service you are being charged for (for example in a workers compensation matter, a personal injury damages claim, a small claim, debt or judgment enforcement, or probate)
      `the fixed cost` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost the regulations fix for that service, in dollars (any number if none is fixed)
      `the amount charged` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount your law practice is charging or seeking to recover for that service, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does a fixed cost stop this charge` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the regulations fix a cost for this legal service`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: s 59(2) speaks only of a cost the regulations fix)
    ELSE IF `the amount charged` GREATER THAN `the fixed cost`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Schedule 1 -- maximum costs in personal injury damages matters`

-- The Act's figures (cl 2(1), cl 3(4)); the local regulations may replace them (cll 2(2), 3(5)), not deposited.
`the Schedule 1 limit on the amount recovered` MEANS 100000
`the Schedule 1 minimum maximum` MEANS 10000
`the Schedule 1 percentage` MEANS 20%
`the clause 3 minimum additional amount` MEANS 7500
`the clause 3 percentage` MEANS 15%

-- cl 8 "(1) A reference in this Schedule to the amount recovered on a claim includes any amount paid under a compromise
-- or settlement of the claim ... (2) ... no regard is to be had to any part of the amount recovered that is
-- attributable to costs or to the addition of interest."
GIVEN `the total paid on the claim` IS A NUMBER
      `the part for costs` IS A NUMBER
      `the part for interest` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount recovered under clause 8` `the total paid on the claim` `the part for costs` `the part for interest` MEANS
    (`the total paid on the claim` MINUS `the part for costs`) MINUS `the part for interest`

-- cl 1(2) "This Schedule does not apply to the following costs" (a flat negative: JUST FALSE); cl 2(1) "If the amount
-- recovered ... does not exceed $100,000" (an "if": JUST FALSE over it). A claim that is not for personal injury damages
-- is outside the Schedule's scope, which has no "only": NOTHING (fork F1). "Personal injury damages" is borrowed from
-- Part 2 of the Civil Liability Act 2002: asked.
GIVEN `it is a claim for personal injury damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of personal injury claim`
      `the amount recovered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 fixes maximum costs for` `it is a claim for personal injury damages` `the kind of claim` `the amount recovered` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a claim for personal injury damages`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": Schedule 1 speaks only of personal injury damages; fork F1)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the kind of claim`
         WHEN `a claim under the Motor Accidents Act 1988 or the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `a claim for work injury damages` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `a dust diseases claim of the kind in section 11 of the Dust Diseases Tribunal Act 1989` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE IF `the amount recovered` GREATER THAN `the Schedule 1 limit on the amount recovered`
                   THEN JUST FALSE
                   ELSE JUST TRUE

@export Does the Schedule 1 maximum costs limit apply to my personal injury damages claim (Sch 1 cll 1, 2(1), 8)?
GIVEN `it is a claim for personal injury damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for personal injury damages within the meaning of Part 2 of the Civil Liability Act 2002 (damages that relate to the death of or injury to a person)
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of personal injury claim` @desc What kind of claim it is. One of: "a claim under the Motor Accidents Act 1988 or the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999", "a claim for work injury damages", "a dust diseases claim of the kind in section 11 of the Dust Diseases Tribunal Act 1989", "a claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017", "another claim for personal injury damages"
      `the total paid on the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount recovered on the claim, in dollars, including any amount paid under a settlement or compromise, whether or not proceedings were started (0 if nothing was recovered)
      `the part of it for costs` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is for costs, in dollars
      `the part of it for interest` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is interest added to the damages, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the maximum costs limit apply to my claim` MEANS
    `Schedule 1 fixes maximum costs for` `it is a claim for personal injury damages` `the kind of claim` (`the amount recovered under clause 8` `the total paid on the claim` `the part of it for costs` `the part of it for interest`)

-- cl 2(1) "(a) ... a plaintiff -- maximum costs are fixed at 20% of the amount recovered or $10,000, whichever is
-- greater, (b) ... a defendant -- ... 20% of the amount sought to be recovered by the plaintiff or $10,000, whichever is
-- greater." cl 2(6) "If proceedings are commenced on a claim, the amount sought to be recovered by the plaintiff is taken
-- to be the amount sought to be proved by the plaintiff at the hearing of the claim."
GIVEN `the side` IS A `My side of the claim`
      `the amount recovered` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount sought` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the clause 2 maximum for` `the side` `the amount recovered` `the amount sought` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the side`
    WHEN `the plaintiff` THEN `the greater of` (`the amount recovered` TIMES `the Schedule 1 percentage`) `and` `the Schedule 1 minimum maximum`
    WHEN `the defendant` THEN `the greater of` (`the amount sought` TIMES `the Schedule 1 percentage`) `and` `the Schedule 1 minimum maximum`

-- cl 3(4) the additional amount: 15% of the amount recovered (plaintiff) or of the amount sought (defendant), or $7,500,
-- whichever is greater.
GIVEN `the side` IS A `My side of the claim`
      `the amount recovered` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount sought` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the clause 3 additional amount for` `the side` `the amount recovered` `the amount sought` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the side`
    WHEN `the plaintiff` THEN `the greater of` (`the amount recovered` TIMES `the clause 3 percentage`) `and` `the clause 3 minimum additional amount`
    WHEN `the defendant` THEN `the greater of` (`the amount sought` TIMES `the clause 3 percentage`) `and` `the clause 3 minimum additional amount`

-- cl 3(1) the clause applies to a claim (amount recovered within the limit) "made by proceedings heard by the District
-- Court". cl 3(2) after arbitration and a rehearing ordered "on the application of a party", the maximum for "the other
-- party" is increased by the additional amount. cl 3(3) on an appeal from the District Court's decision, the
-- respondent's maximum is increased by the additional amount, or by 2 times it if cl 3(2) also applies to the respondent.
GIVEN `heard by the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rehearing on the other side's application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the respondent to an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of clause 3 additional amounts for` `heard by the District Court` `rehearing on the other side's application` `I am the respondent to an appeal` MEANS
    IF (NOT `heard by the District Court`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE (IF `rehearing on the other side's application` THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS (IF `I am the respondent to an appeal` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

GIVEN `it is a claim for personal injury damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of personal injury claim`
      `the side` IS A `My side of the claim`
      `the amount recovered` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount sought` IS A NUMBER
      `heard by the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rehearing on the other side's application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am the respondent to an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Maximum costs answer`
`the Schedule 1 maximum for` `it is a claim for personal injury damages` `the kind of claim` `the side` `the amount recovered` `the amount sought` `heard by the District Court` `rehearing on the other side's application` `I am the respondent to an appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Schedule 1 fixes maximum costs for` `it is a claim for personal injury damages` `the kind of claim` `the amount recovered`
    WHEN JUST b THEN
        IF b
        THEN `the maximum costs are` (`the clause 2 maximum for` `the side` `the amount recovered` `the amount sought` PLUS (`the number of clause 3 additional amounts for` `heard by the District Court` `rehearing on the other side's application` `I am the respondent to an appeal` TIMES `the clause 3 additional amount for` `the side` `the amount recovered` `the amount sought`))
        ELSE `Schedule 1 fixes no maximum for this claim`
    OTHERWISE `the Act does not settle it` -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": not a personal injury damages claim; fork F1)

@export What are the maximum costs for the legal services provided to my side on my personal injury damages claim (Sch 1 cll 2, 3, 8)?
GIVEN `it is a claim for personal injury damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for personal injury damages within the meaning of Part 2 of the Civil Liability Act 2002
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of personal injury claim` @desc What kind of claim it is. One of: "a claim under the Motor Accidents Act 1988 or the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999", "a claim for work injury damages", "a dust diseases claim of the kind in section 11 of the Dust Diseases Tribunal Act 1989", "a claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017", "another claim for personal injury damages"
      `my side` IS A `My side of the claim` @desc Your side of the claim. One of: "the plaintiff" (you claim or are entitled to claim the damages), "the defendant" (the claim is or may be made against you)
      `the total paid on the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount recovered on the claim, in dollars, including any settlement or compromise payment (0 if nothing was recovered)
      `the part of it for costs` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is for costs, in dollars
      `the part of it for interest` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is interest added to the damages, in dollars
      `the amount the plaintiff sought` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the plaintiff sought to recover, in dollars; if proceedings were started, the amount the plaintiff sought to prove at the hearing (cl 2(6))
      `the claim was heard by the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim was made by proceedings heard by the District Court
      `a rehearing after arbitration was ordered on the other side's application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the District Court referred the proceedings to arbitration and then ordered a full or limited rehearing on the application of the other side
      `I am the respondent to an appeal from the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the District Court's decision on the claim has been appealed and you are the respondent to the appeal
GIVETH A `Maximum costs answer`
`What are the maximum costs for my side` MEANS
    `the Schedule 1 maximum for` `it is a claim for personal injury damages` `the kind of claim` `my side` (`the amount recovered under clause 8` `the total paid on the claim` `the part of it for costs` `the part of it for interest`) `the amount the plaintiff sought` `the claim was heard by the District Court` `a rehearing after arbitration was ordered on the other side's application` `I am the respondent to an appeal from the District Court`

-- cl 7 "(1) If more than one law practice provides legal services to a party ... the maximum costs ... are to be
-- apportioned between them as agreed by them or (failing agreement) as ordered by the court ... (2) The maximum then
-- applicable to a particular law practice is the law practice's apportioned share." The share is agreed or ordered: an
-- input.
@export If more than one law practice acts for me (for example a solicitor and a barrister), what is the most one of them may be paid for my personal injury damages claim (Sch 1 cl 7)?
GIVEN `it is a claim for personal injury damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for personal injury damages within the meaning of Part 2 of the Civil Liability Act 2002
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of personal injury claim` @desc What kind of claim it is. One of: "a claim under the Motor Accidents Act 1988 or the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999", "a claim for work injury damages", "a dust diseases claim of the kind in section 11 of the Dust Diseases Tribunal Act 1989", "a claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017", "another claim for personal injury damages"
      `my side` IS A `My side of the claim` @desc Your side of the claim. One of: "the plaintiff", "the defendant"
      `the total paid on the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount recovered on the claim, in dollars, including any settlement or compromise payment (0 if nothing was recovered)
      `the part of it for costs` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is for costs, in dollars
      `the part of it for interest` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is interest added to the damages, in dollars
      `the amount the plaintiff sought` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the plaintiff sought to recover, in dollars; if proceedings were started, the amount the plaintiff sought to prove at the hearing
      `the claim was heard by the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim was made by proceedings heard by the District Court
      `a rehearing after arbitration was ordered on the other side's application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the District Court ordered a rehearing after arbitration on the application of the other side
      `I am the respondent to an appeal from the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the respondent to an appeal from the District Court's decision on the claim
      `that law practice's share in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The share of the maximum costs that the law practices agreed (or the court ordered) for the law practice you are asking about, as a percentage from 0 to 100 (100 if it is the only law practice acting for you)
GIVETH A `Maximum costs answer`
`What is the most one of my law practices may be paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What are the maximum costs for my side` `it is a claim for personal injury damages` `the kind of claim` `my side` `the total paid on the claim` `the part of it for costs` `the part of it for interest` `the amount the plaintiff sought` `the claim was heard by the District Court` `a rehearing after arbitration was ordered on the other side's application` `I am the respondent to an appeal from the District Court`
    WHEN `the maximum costs are` total THEN `the maximum costs are` ((total TIMES `that law practice's share in percent`) DIVIDED BY 100)
    WHEN `Schedule 1 fixes no maximum for this claim` THEN `Schedule 1 fixes no maximum for this claim`
    OTHERWISE `the Act does not settle it` -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only"; fork F1)

-- cl 2(4)(a) "a law practice is not entitled to be paid or recover for those legal services an amount that exceeds
-- those maximum costs", subject to cll 4-6. cl 4(1) "This Schedule does not apply to the recovery of costs payable as
-- between a law practice and the practice's client to the extent that recovery of those costs is provided for by a
-- costs agreement that complies with Division 4 of Part 4.3 of the Legal Profession Uniform Law (NSW)"; cl 4(3) the
-- local regulations may take that benefit away from a practice that failed to comply with their disclosure
-- requirements. cl 6 the court may by order exclude legal services from the Schedule. Whether a costs agreement complies
-- with the Uniform Law, and what the local regulations require, are asked.
@export Does the maximum costs limit stop my own law practice from charging me more than the maximum for my personal injury damages claim (Sch 1 cll 2(4)(a), 4, 6)?
GIVEN `it is a claim for personal injury damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for personal injury damages within the meaning of Part 2 of the Civil Liability Act 2002
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of personal injury claim` @desc What kind of claim it is. One of: "a claim under the Motor Accidents Act 1988 or the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999", "a claim for work injury damages", "a dust diseases claim of the kind in section 11 of the Dust Diseases Tribunal Act 1989", "a claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017", "another claim for personal injury damages"
      `the total paid on the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount recovered on the claim, in dollars, including any settlement or compromise payment (0 if nothing was recovered)
      `the part of it for costs` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is for costs, in dollars
      `the part of it for interest` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is interest added to the damages, in dollars
      `I have a costs agreement with my law practice that provides for those costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a costs agreement with your law practice that complies with Division 4 of Part 4.3 of the Legal Profession Uniform Law and provides for the costs it is charging you
      `the regulations take away my law practice's benefit of the costs agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, under the local regulations made for Schedule 1 clause 4, your law practice has lost the benefit of the costs agreement (for example by not telling you what the agreement means for the maximum costs)
      `the court has excluded these legal services from the maximum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court hearing the claim has ordered under Schedule 1 clause 6 that the legal services you are asking about are excluded from the maximum costs
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the maximum stop my law practice charging me more` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Does the maximum costs limit apply to my claim` `it is a claim for personal injury damages` `the kind of claim` `the total paid on the claim` `the part of it for costs` `the part of it for interest`
    WHEN JUST b THEN
        IF (NOT b)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `the court has excluded these legal services from the maximum`
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE IF     `I have a costs agreement with my law practice that provides for those costs`
                     AND (NOT `the regulations take away my law practice's benefit of the costs agreement`)
                  THEN JUST FALSE
                  ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": not a personal injury damages claim; fork F1)

-- cl 5(2) "An offer of compromise on a claim by a party is reasonable if the court determines or makes an order or award
-- on the claim in terms that are no less favourable to the party than the terms of the offer." Compared on the money
-- terms only (fork F4): a plaintiff's offer (to accept an amount) is no less favourable to the plaintiff when the award is
-- at least the offer; a defendant's offer (to pay an amount) when the award is at most the offer. An "if": with no court
-- determination or award, the offer is not shown reasonable (JUST FALSE).
GIVEN `the offering side` IS A `My side of the claim`
      `the offer amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the court has determined the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount awarded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offer of compromise is reasonable` `the offering side` `the offer amount` `the court has determined the claim` `the amount awarded` IF
        `the court has determined the claim`
    AND CONSIDER `the offering side`
        WHEN `the plaintiff` THEN `the amount awarded` AT LEAST `the offer amount`
        WHEN `the defendant` THEN `the amount awarded` AT MOST `the offer amount`

GIVEN `the side` IS A `My side of the claim`
GIVETH A `My side of the claim`
`the other side to` `the side` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the side`
    WHEN `the plaintiff` THEN `the defendant`
    WHEN `the defendant` THEN `the plaintiff`

-- cl 2(4)(b) "a court or tribunal cannot order the payment by another party to the claim of costs in respect of those
-- legal services in an amount that exceeds that maximum", subject to cll 5 and 6. cl 5(1) "If a party ... makes a
-- reasonable offer of compromise on the claim that is not accepted, this Schedule does not prevent the awarding of costs
-- against another party to be assessed on an indemnity basis in respect of legal services provided after the offer is
-- made." Answer JUST TRUE: the maximum protects the paying party; JUST FALSE: on these facts the Schedule does not stop
-- the order (whether the court makes it is the court's).
GIVEN `it is a claim for personal injury damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of personal injury claim`
      `the amount recovered` IS A NUMBER
      `the offering side` IS A `My side of the claim`
      `an offer was made and not accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the court has determined the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount awarded` IS A NUMBER
      `the services were provided after the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the services are excluded by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the maximum limits the costs order for` `it is a claim for personal injury damages` `the kind of claim` `the amount recovered` `the offering side` `an offer was made and not accepted` `the offer amount` `the court has determined the claim` `the amount awarded` `the services were provided after the offer` `the services are excluded by the court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Schedule 1 fixes maximum costs for` `it is a claim for personal injury damages` `the kind of claim` `the amount recovered`
    WHEN JUST b THEN
        IF (NOT b)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `the services are excluded by the court`
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE IF     `an offer was made and not accepted`
                     AND `the services were provided after the offer`
                     AND `the offer of compromise is reasonable` `the offering side` `the offer amount` `the court has determined the claim` `the amount awarded`
                  THEN JUST FALSE
                  ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": not a personal injury damages claim; fork F1)

@export Does the maximum costs limit stop the court ordering me to pay the other side's costs above the other side's maximum (Sch 1 cll 2(4)(b), 5, 6)?
GIVEN `it is a claim for personal injury damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for personal injury damages within the meaning of Part 2 of the Civil Liability Act 2002
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of personal injury claim` @desc What kind of claim it is. One of: "a claim under the Motor Accidents Act 1988 or the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999", "a claim for work injury damages", "a dust diseases claim of the kind in section 11 of the Dust Diseases Tribunal Act 1989", "a claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017", "another claim for personal injury damages"
      `my side` IS A `My side of the claim` @desc Your side of the claim. One of: "the plaintiff", "the defendant"
      `the total paid on the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount recovered on the claim, in dollars, including any settlement or compromise payment (0 if nothing was recovered)
      `the part of it for costs` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is for costs, in dollars
      `the part of it for interest` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is interest added to the damages, in dollars
      `the other side made an offer of compromise I did not accept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other side made an offer of compromise on the claim that you did not accept
      `the amount of that offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the other side offered to accept (if they are the plaintiff) or to pay (if they are the defendant), in dollars
      `the court has determined the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has determined the claim or made an order or award on it
      `the amount the court awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the court's determination, order or award on the claim, in dollars (0 if nothing was awarded)
      `the costs are for legal services after the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other side's costs you are asking about are for legal services provided after that offer was made
      `the court has excluded those services from the maximum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has ordered under Schedule 1 clause 6 that those legal services to the other side are excluded from the maximum (because they answered an action on your side that was not reasonably necessary or was meant or likely to delay or complicate the claim)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the maximum protect me from paying the other side more` MEANS
    `the maximum limits the costs order for` `it is a claim for personal injury damages` `the kind of claim` (`the amount recovered under clause 8` `the total paid on the claim` `the part of it for costs` `the part of it for interest`) (`the other side to` `my side`) `the other side made an offer of compromise I did not accept` `the amount of that offer` `the court has determined the claim` `the amount the court awarded` `the costs are for legal services after the offer` `the court has excluded those services from the maximum`

@export Does the maximum costs limit stop the court ordering the other side to pay my costs above my maximum (Sch 1 cll 2(4)(b), 5, 6)?
GIVEN `it is a claim for personal injury damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for personal injury damages within the meaning of Part 2 of the Civil Liability Act 2002
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of personal injury claim` @desc What kind of claim it is. One of: "a claim under the Motor Accidents Act 1988 or the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999", "a claim for work injury damages", "a dust diseases claim of the kind in section 11 of the Dust Diseases Tribunal Act 1989", "a claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017", "another claim for personal injury damages"
      `my side` IS A `My side of the claim` @desc Your side of the claim. One of: "the plaintiff", "the defendant"
      `the total paid on the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount recovered on the claim, in dollars, including any settlement or compromise payment (0 if nothing was recovered)
      `the part of it for costs` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is for costs, in dollars
      `the part of it for interest` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that total is interest added to the damages, in dollars
      `I made an offer of compromise the other side did not accept` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made an offer of compromise on the claim that the other side did not accept
      `the amount of my offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you offered to accept (if you are the plaintiff) or to pay (if you are the defendant), in dollars
      `the court has determined the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has determined the claim or made an order or award on it
      `the amount the court awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the court's determination, order or award on the claim, in dollars (0 if nothing was awarded)
      `the costs are for legal services after my offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your costs you are asking about are for legal services provided after your offer was made
      `the court has excluded those services from the maximum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has ordered under Schedule 1 clause 6 that those legal services to you are excluded from the maximum
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the maximum limit what the other side can be ordered to pay me` MEANS
    `the maximum limits the costs order for` `it is a claim for personal injury damages` `the kind of claim` (`the amount recovered under clause 8` `the total paid on the claim` `the part of it for costs` `the part of it for interest`) `my side` `I made an offer of compromise the other side did not accept` `the amount of my offer` `the court has determined the claim` `the amount the court awarded` `the costs are for legal services after my offer` `the court has excluded those services from the maximum`

-- cl 5(4) "If it appears to the court ... that a law practice has failed to comply with any provision of the local
-- regulations under this clause, and that the client ... has incurred an increased liability for costs as a result of
-- refusing a reasonable offer of compromise ..., the court may ... make ... (a) an order directing the law practice to
-- repay to the client the whole or any part of those increased costs". The court's power is a "may": JUST TRUE means it
-- may; an unmet "if" condition is JUST FALSE. The disclosure the local regulations require (cl 5(3)) is not deposited:
-- asked.
@export Can the court order my law practice to repay me the extra costs I was ordered to pay because I refused a reasonable offer of compromise (Sch 1 cl 5(4))?
GIVEN `it is a claim for personal injury damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for personal injury damages within the meaning of Part 2 of the Civil Liability Act 2002
      `my side` IS A `My side of the claim` @desc Your side of the claim. One of: "the plaintiff", "the defendant"
      `I refused an offer of compromise from the other side` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you refused an offer of compromise the other side made on the claim
      `the amount of that offer` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the other side offered to accept (if they are the plaintiff) or to pay (if they are the defendant), in dollars
      `the court has determined the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has determined the claim or made an order or award on it
      `the amount the court awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the court's determination, order or award on the claim, in dollars
      `I was ordered to pay increased costs because I refused it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have incurred an increased liability for costs (been ordered to pay more of the other side's costs) as a result of refusing that offer
      `my law practice failed to give me the information the regulations require about offers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your law practice failed to comply with the local regulations made under Schedule 1 clause 5 (which may require it to tell you what refusing an offer of compromise can mean for costs)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court make my law practice repay the extra costs of refusing the offer` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a claim for personal injury damages`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": cl 5(4) speaks of a claim for personal injury damages; fork F1)
    ELSE IF     `I refused an offer of compromise from the other side`
            AND `the offer of compromise is reasonable` (`the other side to` `my side`) `the amount of that offer` `the court has determined the claim` `the amount the court awarded`
            AND `I was ordered to pay increased costs because I refused it`
            AND `my law practice failed to give me the information the regulations require about offers`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Schedule 2 -- costs in civil claims where there are no reasonable prospects of success`

-- cl 2(1) "A law practice must not provide legal services on a claim or defence of a claim for damages unless a legal
-- practitioner associate responsible for the provision of the services concerned reasonably believes on the basis of
-- provable facts and a reasonably arguable view of the law that the claim or the defence ... has reasonable prospects of
-- success." cl 2(3) it applies despite the client's instructions. cl 3 "This Schedule does not apply to legal services
-- provided as a preliminary matter for the purpose of a proper and reasonable consideration of whether a claim or defence
-- has reasonable prospects of success." The associate's belief is a judgment: asked. "Must not ... unless": JUST FALSE
-- when the belief is not held. A matter that is not a claim for damages is outside the Schedule (NOTHING).
@export Can my law practice act for me on my claim (or my defence of a claim) for damages, given what it believes about my prospects of success (Sch 2 cll 2, 3)?
GIVEN `it is a claim or a defence of a claim for damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal services are on a claim for damages, or on the defence of a claim for damages (in a court at first instance or on appeal)
      `the work is only a preliminary look at my prospects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the legal services are only preliminary work to consider properly and reasonably whether your claim or defence has reasonable prospects of success
      `the responsible lawyer reasonably believes my case has reasonable prospects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lawyer responsible for the work reasonably believes, on the basis of provable facts and a reasonably arguable view of the law, that your claim has reasonable prospects of recovering damages (or your defence of defeating the claim or reducing the damages)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my law practice act on my claim or defence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a claim or a defence of a claim for damages`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": Schedule 2 speaks of claims for damages)
    ELSE IF `the work is only a preliminary look at my prospects`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the responsible lawyer reasonably believes my case has reasonable prospects`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- cl 4(2) "A law practice cannot file court documentation on a claim or defence of a claim for damages unless a principal
-- of the practice, or a legal practitioner associate responsible ..., certifies that there are reasonable grounds for
-- believing ... that the claim or the defence ... has reasonable prospects of success." cl 4(3) it "is not to be filed ...
-- unless accompanied by the certification". cl 4(4) defines "court documentation". A document outside the definition is
-- not reached (NOTHING); with the certificate, Schedule 2 does not stop the filing (JUST TRUE).
@export Can my law practice file this court document on my claim (or defence) for damages (Sch 2 cl 4)?
GIVEN `it is a claim or a defence of a claim for damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document is on a claim for damages or on the defence of a claim for damages
      `the kind of document` IS A `Kind of court document` @desc The kind of document. One of: "an originating process, defence or further pleading" (for example a statement of claim, summons or cross-claim), "an amended originating process, defence or further pleading", "a document amending an originating process, defence or further pleading", "another document of a kind the local regulations prescribe", "any other document"
      `it has the reasonable prospects certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a principal of your law practice, or the lawyer responsible, has certified that there are reasonable grounds for believing, on provable facts and a reasonably arguable view of the law, that your claim or defence has reasonable prospects of success, and the certificate accompanies the document
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my court document be filed` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a claim or a defence of a claim for damages`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": Schedule 2 speaks of claims for damages)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the kind of document`
         WHEN `any other document` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: cl 4 speaks only of court documentation as cl 4(4) defines it)
         OTHERWISE IF `it has the reasonable prospects certificate`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE

-- cl 6(1) a presumption that services were provided without reasonable prospects of success arises where the trial
-- court finds the facts established by the evidence do not form a basis for a reasonable belief that the claim or
-- defence had reasonable prospects; cl 6(2) the same where the Supreme Court (not the trial court) is so satisfied;
-- cl 6(3) it is rebuttable.
GIVEN `the trial court found no basis for a reasonable belief in prospects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Supreme Court is satisfied there was no such basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the presumption has been rebutted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the clause 6 presumption stands` `the trial court found no basis for a reasonable belief in prospects` `the Supreme Court is satisfied there was no such basis` `the presumption has been rebutted` IF
        (   `the trial court found no basis for a reasonable belief in prospects`
         OR `the Supreme Court is satisfied there was no such basis`)
    AND (NOT `the presumption has been rebutted`)

-- cl 5(1) "If it appears to a court ... that a law practice has provided legal services to a party without reasonable
-- prospects of success, the court may of its own motion or on the application of any party ... make ... (a) an order
-- directing the practice or associate to repay to the party to whom the services were provided the whole or any part of
-- the costs that the party has been ordered to pay to any other party". cl 5(3) "An application for an order under this
-- clause cannot be made after a final determination has been made under Part 7 by a costs assessor of the costs payable
-- as a result of an order made by the court". An application made on the day of the final determination is taken as not
-- "after" it (fork F5). Whether it "appears" to the court is the court's: the presumption of cl 6 or the court's own
-- finding, both asked.
@export If I lost and was ordered to pay the other side's costs, can I ask the court to order my law practice to repay them because it acted without reasonable prospects of success (Sch 2 cll 5, 6)?
GIVEN `it is a claim or a defence of a claim for damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceedings are on a claim for damages (yours or one you defended)
      `I was ordered to pay costs to another party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been ordered to pay costs to another party in the proceedings
      `the trial court found no basis for a reasonable belief in prospects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trial court found that the facts established by the evidence do not form a basis for a reasonable belief that your claim or defence had reasonable prospects of success
      `the Supreme Court is satisfied there was no such basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court (not being the trial court) is satisfied, from the trial court's finding or judgment, that there was no such basis
      `my law practice has rebutted the presumption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your law practice has shown that, when it acted, there were provable facts giving a basis for a reasonable belief that your claim or defence had reasonable prospects of success
      `the court otherwise finds my law practice acted without reasonable prospects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, apart from that presumption, it appears to the court that your law practice provided legal services to you without reasonable prospects of success
      `a costs assessor has made a final determination of those costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a costs assessor has made a final determination under Part 7 of the Act of the costs payable under the court's order
      `the day of that final determination` IS A DATE @desc The day the costs assessor made that final determination (any day if there is none)
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply (or applied) to the court for the order
GIVETH A `Repayment order answer`
`Can I seek repayment of the costs from my law practice` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a claim or a defence of a claim for damages`)
    THEN `Schedule 2 does not reach my claim` -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": Schedule 2 speaks of claims for damages)
    ELSE IF     `a costs assessor has made a final determination of those costs`
            AND `the days from` `the day of that final determination` `to` `the day I apply` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `it is too late to apply for that order`
         ELSE IF     `I was ordered to pay costs to another party`
                 AND (   `the clause 6 presumption stands` `the trial court found no basis for a reasonable belief in prospects` `the Supreme Court is satisfied there was no such basis` `my law practice has rebutted the presumption`
                      OR `the court otherwise finds my law practice acted without reasonable prospects`)
              THEN `the court may order my law practice to repay those costs`
              ELSE `the court cannot make that order on these facts`

-- cl 5(4) "A law practice or legal practitioner associate of the practice is not entitled to demand, recover or accept
-- from a client any part of the amount for which the practice or associate is directed to indemnify a party pursuant to
-- an order under this clause." A flat negative.
@export If the court ordered my law practice to indemnify the other side for costs because it acted without reasonable prospects of success, can my law practice make me pay any of that amount (Sch 2 cl 5(4))?
GIVEN `my law practice was ordered to indemnify another party under Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court directed your law practice (or its lawyer) under Schedule 2 clause 5 to indemnify another party against costs
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my law practice pass the indemnity on to me` MEANS
    IF `my law practice was ordered to indemnify another party under Schedule 2`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: cl 5(4) speaks only of an amount under such an order)

§§ `Part 7 -- costs assessment`

-- s 63 "ordered costs means costs payable under an order or rule of a court or tribunal". s 66 costs "may be the
-- subject of assessment if the costs assessment rules, the relevant court or tribunal, the rules of the relevant court
-- or tribunal or other legislation so provides" (an "if": JUST FALSE when nothing so provides). s 74(1) "An application
-- for assessment ... of ordered costs may be made by (a) a person who has paid or is liable to pay those costs, or (b) a
-- person who has received or is entitled to receive those costs." An open list: neither is NOTHING.
@export Can I apply for an assessment of costs that a court or tribunal ordered to be paid (ss 63, 66, 74)?
GIVEN `the costs are payable under a court or tribunal order or rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs are payable under an order or rule of a court or tribunal (ordered costs)
      `the rules, the court or other legislation provide for their assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs assessment rules, the court or tribunal, its rules or other legislation provide for these costs to be assessed
      `my position on the costs` IS A `My position on the ordered costs` @desc Your position. One of: "I have paid or am liable to pay them", "I have received or am entitled to receive them", "neither"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply for assessment of ordered costs` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the costs are payable under a court or tribunal order or rule`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": s 74 speaks of ordered costs; Uniform Law costs are assessed under the Uniform Law)
    ELSE IF (NOT `the rules, the court or other legislation provide for their assessment`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `my position on the costs`
              WHEN `neither` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (an open list: s 74(1) does not say "only")
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ss 68(3) and 83(4) "The Manager, Costs Assessment may waive or postpone payment of the application fee either wholly
-- or in part if satisfied that the applicant is in such circumstances that payment of the fee would result in serious
-- hardship to the applicant or his or her dependants." The Manager's satisfaction is asked. JUST TRUE: the Manager may
-- waive or postpone (not that it will).
@export Can the fee for my application for costs assessment or review be waived or postponed because paying it would cause serious hardship (ss 68(3), 83(4))?
GIVEN `paying the fee would cause serious hardship to me or my dependants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Manager, Costs Assessment is satisfied that paying the application fee would result in serious hardship to you or your dependants
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my application fee be waived` MEANS
    IF `paying the fee would cause serious hardship to me or my dependants`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 70(4) "In the case of an amount of money specified in a certificate that has been paid, the amount (if any) by which
-- the amount paid exceeds the amount specified in the certificate may be recovered as a debt in a court of competent
-- jurisdiction." s 87(2) the same for a review panel's certificate.
@export If I paid more costs than the costs assessment certificate specifies, how much can I recover as a debt (ss 70(4), 87(2))?
GIVEN `the amount I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you paid towards the costs the certificate deals with, in dollars
      `the amount in the certificate` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount specified in the costs assessor's (or review panel's) certificate, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much overpaid can I recover` MEANS
    IF `the amount I paid` GREATER THAN `the amount in the certificate`
    THEN `the amount I paid` MINUS `the amount in the certificate`
    ELSE 0

-- s 70(5) "In the case of an amount of money specified in a certificate that has not been paid, the certificate is, on
-- the filing of the certificate in the office or registry of a court having jurisdiction to order the payment of that
-- amount of money, and with no further action, taken to be a judgment of that court for the amount of unpaid money."
@export If an amount in a costs assessment certificate is unpaid, is the certificate now a judgment of a court for it (s 70(5))?
GIVEN `the unpaid amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount specified in the certificate that has not been paid, in dollars
      `the certificate has been filed in a court with jurisdiction for that amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the certificate has been filed in the office or registry of a court that has jurisdiction to order payment of that amount
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the certificate a judgment` MEANS
    IF `the unpaid amount` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: s 70(5) speaks only of an amount not paid)
    ELSE IF `the certificate has been filed in a court with jurisdiction for that amount`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 81(1) "A costs assessor may, in respect of the amount of Uniform Law costs ..., determine that (a) interest is
-- payable at a rate ... that does not exceed the rate referred to in section 195(4) of the Legal Profession Uniform Law
-- (NSW), or (b) no interest is payable." s 81(2) despite any costs agreement. A grant limited in its own words: above
-- the cap the Act does not answer in its own words (NOTHING, under the ruling of 2026-10-29). The s 195(4) rate is the
-- Uniform Law's: asked.
@export Can the costs assessor set this rate of interest on the legal costs I owe my law practice (s 81)?
GIVEN `the rate set` IS A NUMBER @desc The yearly interest rate the costs assessor would set on the Uniform Law costs, as a percentage (0 for no interest)
      `the Uniform Law section 195(4) rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate referred to in section 195(4) of the Legal Profession Uniform Law, as a yearly percentage
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the assessor set this interest rate` MEANS
    IF `the rate set` AT MOST `the Uniform Law section 195(4) rate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited in its own wording, and the case falls outside the limit)

-- s 83(1) "A party to a costs assessment may, within 30 days after the certificate of determination by the costs
-- assessor has been forwarded to the parties ..., apply for a review of the determination." s 83(1A) "The Manager, Costs
-- Assessment may extend the period". Counted under the Interpretation Act 1987 s 36(1), excluding the day of forwarding:
-- the 30th day after it is the last day (fork F6; the next-business-day rule is not applied, fork F7). A period the
-- text fixes: outside it, the time has passed.
`the review period in days` MEANS 30

GIVEN `the day the certificate was forwarded` IS A DATE
      `the Manager extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for review after` `the day the certificate was forwarded` `the Manager extended the period` `the extended last day` MEANS
    IF `the Manager extended the period`
    THEN `the extended last day`
    ELSE `the day the certificate was forwarded` `plus days` `the review period in days`

@export By what day must I apply for a review of the costs assessor's determination (s 83(1), (1A))?
GIVEN `the day the certificate was forwarded` IS A DATE @desc The day the costs assessor's certificate of determination was forwarded to the parties under the regulations or the costs assessment rules
      `the Manager extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Manager, Costs Assessment has extended the period for applying for review
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended period (any day if there is no extension)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for a review` MEANS
    `the last day for review after` `the day the certificate was forwarded` `the Manager extended the period` `the extended last day`

-- The period as a rule: time 0 is the day the certificate was forwarded. (Jurally the party has a power to apply, not a
-- duty; the rule models losing it as LEST BREACH.)
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Costs party` `Costs act`
`s 83 -- a party must apply for review within the period` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the party to the costs assessment`
    MUST `apply for a review of the determination`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST BREACH BY `the party to the costs assessment` BECAUSE "application for review made after the period in s 83(1), as extended under s 83(1A)"

@export Is my application for a review of the costs assessor's determination in time (s 83(1), (1A))?
GIVEN `the day the certificate was forwarded` IS A DATE @desc The day the costs assessor's certificate of determination was forwarded to the parties
      `the Manager extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Manager, Costs Assessment has extended the period for applying for review
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended period (any day if there is no extension)
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you filed (or will file) your application for review with the Manager, Costs Assessment
GIVETH A `Review application answer`
`Is my review application in time` MEANS
    IF `the day applied` LESS THAN 0
    THEN `the certificate has not been forwarded yet, so the 30 days have not begun`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 83 -- a party must apply for review within the period` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day applied`), (EVENT `the party to the costs assessment` `apply for a review of the determination` `the day applied`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `my application for review is in time`
         OTHERWISE `the time for applying for review has passed`
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the days from` `the day the certificate was forwarded` `to` (`the last day for review after` `the day the certificate was forwarded` `the Manager extended the period` `the extended last day`)
        `the day applied` MEANS `the days from` `the day the certificate was forwarded` `to` `the day I apply`

-- s 86(1) "If an application is made to a review panel to review a costs assessor's determination under section 83 or
-- 84, the operation of the determination is suspended." s 86(2) the panel may end the suspension. s 90(1) while an appeal
-- or leave application is pending in the District Court, the review panel or the District Court may suspend the
-- determination or decision; s 90(3) the suspension ends when the appeal is determined or the leave application ends.
@export Is the costs assessor's determination (or the review panel's decision) suspended, so that it does not yet operate against me (ss 86, 90)?
GIVEN `a review of the determination has been applied for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an application has been made (by a party or the Manager, Costs Assessment) for a review of the costs assessor's determination
      `the review panel has ended that suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the review panel has ended the suspension (for example by affirming the determination)
      `the review panel or District Court suspended it pending an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while an appeal (or an application for leave to appeal) is pending in the District Court, the review panel or the District Court ordered the determination or decision suspended
      `that appeal suspension has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that suspension has ended (the appeal was determined, the leave application was dismissed, discontinued, struck out or lapsed, or the suspension was ended)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the determination suspended` MEANS
    IF     `a review of the determination has been applied for`
       AND (NOT `the review panel has ended that suspension`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF     `the review panel or District Court suspended it pending an appeal`
            AND (NOT `that appeal suspension has ended`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 89(1) "A party to a costs assessment that has been the subject of a review under this Part may appeal against a
-- decision of the review panel concerned to (a) the District Court ..., but only with the leave of the Court if the
-- amount of costs in dispute is less than $25,000, or (b) the Supreme Court ..., but only with the leave of the Court if
-- the amount of costs in dispute is less than $100,000." No review: s 89 gives no appeal ("that has been the subject of a
-- review" is the condition of the grant; fork F8).
`the District Court leave threshold` MEANS 25000
`the Supreme Court leave threshold` MEANS 100000

@export Can I appeal against the review panel's decision on my costs, and do I need the court's leave (s 89(1))?
GIVEN `my costs assessment was reviewed by a review panel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs assessment you were a party to has been the subject of a review by a review panel under Part 7
      `the court I appeal to` IS A `Appeal court` @desc The court you would appeal to. One of: "the District Court", "the Supreme Court"
      `the amount of costs in dispute` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of costs in dispute on the appeal, in dollars
GIVETH A `Appeal answer`
`Can I appeal the review panel's decision` MEANS
    IF (NOT `my costs assessment was reviewed by a review panel`)
    THEN `section 89 gives me no appeal`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the court I appeal to`
         WHEN `the District Court` THEN
             IF `the amount of costs in dispute` LESS THAN `the District Court leave threshold`
             THEN `I can appeal only with the court's leave`
             ELSE `I can appeal without leave`
         WHEN `the Supreme Court` THEN
             IF `the amount of costs in dispute` LESS THAN `the Supreme Court leave threshold`
             THEN `I can appeal only with the court's leave`
             ELSE `I can appeal without leave`

§§ `Part 9 Division 2 -- claims against the Fidelity Fund`

-- s 122(1) "A person who suffers pecuniary loss because of a default to which Part 4.5 of the Legal Profession Uniform
-- Law (NSW) applies may make a claim against the Fidelity Fund to the Law Society about the default." s 122(2) "A claim
-- is to be made in writing in a form approved by the Law Society Council." s 124 "Part 4.5 of the Legal Profession
-- Uniform Law (NSW) does not apply to a default of a law practice consisting of a barrister." Whether Part 4.5 would
-- otherwise apply is the Uniform Law's: asked. A grant limited in its own words: no pecuniary loss is NOTHING.
@export Can I make a claim against the Legal Practitioners Fidelity Fund for a loss caused by a law practice's default (ss 122, 124)?
GIVEN `I suffered pecuniary loss because of the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered a money loss because of the law practice's default (for example a failure to account for or pay trust money, or a fraudulent dealing with your property)
      `Part 4.5 of the Uniform Law covers the default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the default is one to which Part 4.5 (fidelity cover) of the Legal Profession Uniform Law applies, apart from s 124 of this Act
      `the law practice is a barrister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the law practice that defaulted consists of a barrister
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I claim against the Fidelity Fund` MEANS
    IF `the law practice is a barrister`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (NOT `Part 4.5 of the Uniform Law covers the default`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `I suffered pecuniary loss because of the default`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited in its own wording, and the case falls outside the limit)
